pocket-motion-only: a colour filter is applied to a filter layer (0018) — a span of the draw list rendered offscreen, read back and composited — which no upstream backend draws; a stream carrying LAYER_PUSH stops there on every upstream target.

0065 — colour filters: CSS's `brightness`, `contrast`, `grayscale`,
`hue-rotate`, `invert`, `saturate` and `sepia`, as Tailwind classes, as
keyframe properties and in a keyframe `filter` list.

Each is the colour matrix Filter Effects 1 gives the function, applied to
the node's filter layer — the node and its whole subtree — on straight-alpha
colour, after the layer's blur and before its shadow: the place Tailwind's
`filter` composition gives them, in its order (brightness, contrast,
grayscale, hue-rotate, invert, saturate, sepia) whatever order the classes
are written in. Each result is clamped to 0..1 before the next, as each CSS
filter primitive's is, so `brightness(2) contrast(0.5)` is not one matrix.
Alpha is untouched: a shadow or glow, made from alpha, keeps its own colour,
and a luma glow (0033) reads the filtered colour.

Fixed point, integer: a 3x3 matrix in 1/16384ths and an offset, on channels
held as c * 257 (0..65535, so 8-bit levels map in and out exactly), each
step rounded and clamped in i64. The coefficients come from the amount by
f32 arithmetic and the core's own `sinf`/`cosf` (fmath.rs), then rounded, so
the words alone decide the pixels on every host. Hue-rotate is reduced to
0..360 degrees first, so a whole turn is identity to the bit. Amounts are
clamped as CSS clamps them — grayscale, invert and sepia at 1, a negative
amount to 0 — and brightness, contrast and saturate at COLOR_FILTER_MAX
(256), past which every 8-bit channel is a threshold already.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, the regenerated `spec.rs`, the
  microts spec and component types: props `brightness` .. `sepia`
  (212-218, f32), animatable at bits 66-72 (timeline and `animate()`);
  `COLOR_FILTER` (each filter's order and bit), `COLOR_FILTER_MAX`; LAYER_PUSH
  documented as 8 + k words — bits 24-30 of the blend word name the filters
  present, and one f32 amount per set bit follows the eighth word. A layer
  with no colour filter is the eight words it was.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the seven fields, CSS's identities as defaults.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `color_filters` clamps the amounts and masks
  out every filter at identity; any left makes the node layered.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `layer_push_len`; `ColorStep` (one filter's
  quantised matrix) and `ColorProgram` (the layer's, decoded from the op);
  `composite_layer` runs it after the blur over the content rectangle,
  computing a colour once per run of equal pixels. And the layer's bounds:
  `LayerTarget` records the columns it touched beside the rows, so the alpha
  scan and the pool's clear cover the touched rectangle and not whole rows,
  and `composite_layer` returns that rectangle. A word-sized layer at 1080p
  had scanned and cleared 1920-pixel rows: 0.20 to 0.05 ms a layer native,
  byte-identical, for every filter layer.
- `compositor.rs`, `damage.rs`, `lib.rs`: each draw-list walker takes
  LAYER_PUSH's length from `layer_push_len`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `grayscale`, `sepia`, `invert`;
  `<filter>-N` as N percent and `hue-rotate-N` / `-hue-rotate-N` as degrees;
  `<filter>-[x]` as a CSS amount or, for hue-rotate, a CSS angle (deg, grad,
  rad, turn). Negative amounts, an angle with no unit and a brightness,
  contrast or saturate past 256 do not parse.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: `COLOR_FILTERS`, `filterAmount`,
  `filterAngle`; the seven as keyframe properties by function name
  (`hueRotate`); and `filter` lists as CSS interpolates them — a keyframe
  that writes `filter` pins every function any keyframe names, at its
  initial value where it does not name it (`none` included, a missing
  drop-shadow fading to its colour at alpha 0); a list out of the one order
  (blur, the colour filters, drop-shadow), a function named twice, and two
  neighbouring lists neither a prefix of the other — which CSS interpolates
  discretely — are refused, as is a prop set both by a `filter` and by its
  own keyframe property. Until now a keyframe that named fewer functions
  left the rest unpinned there; no composition in pocket-motion's tree
  wrote such a list.

Layer or draw time was measured, not assumed (pocket-motion
`baselines/colour-filters.md`; `colour_filter_layer_cost` below, ignored,
reproduces the native half). A draw-time recolour would save the layer's
cost, now about 0.05 ms a word-sized node native, and is exact only for a
subtree of one op that cannot overlap itself: where two ops of the subtree
cover one pixel, two blends round differently from the layer's one, and a
text run's glyphs meet in pixels. So a colour filter is always a layer.

Guards (`engine/core/src/tests.rs`), each watched red under the edit named:
`each_colour_filter_is_its_css_matrix_to_a_level` — every function at three
to five amounts over seven colours within 0.55 of a level of an f64
transcription of the spec (measured worst 0.504); red with a grayscale
coefficient 0.7152 written 0.7125, and with a hue-rotate one 0.140 written
0.104, which the +-1 comparison it replaced let through.
`colour_filters_apply_in_tailwinds_order_each_clamped` — red with the clamp
moved to after the last step (and the canonical order against the
reference). `a_colour_filter_at_identity_is_no_layer_and_a_whole_turn_is_identity`
— red with the identity mask removed, and with hue's reduction removed.
`a_colour_filter_leaves_alpha_and_the_shadow_alone` — red with the shadow's
colour filtered. `a_colour_filter_applies_to_the_blurred_picture` — red with
the pass before the blur (a black and white split under contrast(8), which
before a blur changes nothing). `a_colour_filter_reaches_everything_the_blur_spread`
— red with the pass over the unblurred rectangle.
`every_draw_list_walker_steps_over_a_colour_filtered_layer` — a sibling and
a compositor surface after a colour-filtered layer; red with the length left
at 8 in compositor.rs, in damage.rs, and in lib.rs's
`compositor_surface_frames`. `validate_drawlist` holds the
blend word's new bits and every amount's range. Vendored
`tests/tailwind.test.ts` pins the compiler, its refusals included.

Ledgers, measured when this was 0055 on main at 524173f, before
0045-0059, against what main had recorded: no existing digest
and no existing `visibility` row moves — 42 compositions, `filters`,
`bloom`, `stroke`, `shutter-blur` and every other one that draws a filter
layer among them, so the column-bounded layer is byte-identical where it is
used. `compositions/colour-filters` is new in both: 30 frames; 25 nodes, 13
named, every one shown.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

